 "verdict": "n_candidates alone scores AUROC 0.2733, so group size DOES encode the per-group base rate and part of the block is design leakage. the block is worth +0.0836 AUPRC under the benchmark's candidate definition and +0.0713 under the genome-wide one (difference +0.0123). training on one definition and scoring the other -- which is what the shipped edge layer does -- costs -0.1201 AUPRC. 16% of the gain is the within-group ORDERING (destroyed by a within-group shuffle); the remainder survives it and is therefore not ordering information at all."
